Parent programme: #740.
Direct parents: QG-12 SixLCU all-instance P0 label theorem; QG-15b frozen-predicate-language calibration.
ORION-Q transfer parent: MAX-R4E #903.

## Status

**PROSPECTIVE DIFFERENT-FAMILY TARGET. FREEZE BEFORE ANY QG-33 GAP-FIBER OUTCOME.**

Existing earned facts must remain unchanged:
- QG-12: for frozen SixLCU, `C_F == C_U iff P0` all admitted instances/all n.
- QG-15b on complete n=2 SixLCU domain: a one-literal frozen-vocabulary predicate at K1D1 exactly classifies the donor-optimal label (`E_floor=0`).

These are **label** results. QG-33 asks a richer value question:

> Does the same minimal label abstraction also determine the exact optimization improvement magnitude `Delta = C_U - C_F`, or do identical label-abstraction states contain multiple exact gap values?

No outcome is frozen.

## Q1 — complete frozen n=2 gap census

Use exactly the committed QG-4/QG-15b complete n=2 SixLCU universe and production evaluator. For every instance compute:
- `C_U` donor cost;
- `C_F` exact frozen-family optimum;
- `Delta = C_U - C_F >= 0`;
- the exact frozen one-literal K1D1 classifier selected/authorized by QG-15b;
- QG-12/P0 label as an independent label binding.

Required counts:
- total instances;
- exact `Delta` histogram;
- label confusion against QG-12/P0;
- per-one-literal-cell `Delta` histograms.

## Q2 — label-abstraction value sufficiency

Define `A_label` as the binary output of the minimal exact one-literal donor-optimal classifier.

Test exact value sufficiency:

`VALUE_SUFFICIENT(A_label) := Delta is constant on every A_label equivalence class.`

If false, serialize the lexicographically first pair of instances with:
- identical `A_label`;
- different exact `Delta`;
- both exact costs;
- frozen feature vectors;
- QG-12/P0 labels.

Allowed positive separation terminal:
`QG33_SIXLCU_EXACT_LABEL_QUOTIENT_IS_NOT_EXACT_VALUE_QUOTIENT__N2_COMPLETE`

Honest alternative:
`QG33_SIXLCU_ONE_LITERAL_LABEL_QUOTIENT_ALSO_VALUE_SUFFICIENT__N2_COMPLETE`

Either outcome is bounded to the complete frozen n=2 domain unless a separate symbolic theorem is added later.

## Q3 — frozen feature-vector value floor

Using the complete frozen **QG-15b SixLCU feature vector** (not arbitrary new features), group n=2 instances by identical feature vector and compute:
- number of feature cells;
- mixed-`Delta` cell count;
- irreducible exact-value prediction floor under this frozen feature vocabulary: `sum_cell (cell_size - max_delta_frequency_in_cell)`;
- first mixed-value cell if any.

This distinguishes:
- one-literal label insufficiency only;
- full frozen-vocabulary information insufficiency.

Do not search a new feature language in QG-33.

## Q4 — query-indexed abstraction interpretation

QG-33 may authorize only the exact compiler-specific relation between:
- donor-optimal **label** query;
- exact improvement **value** query;
- the frozen one-literal and full-feature abstractions.

If label abstraction is value-insufficient, this is a cross-family confirmation of QG-31's query-indexed-authority lesson: an abstraction exact for one scientific question can be invalid for a richer one.

If the full frozen feature vector is also value-insufficient, register a successor state-vocabulary lane; do not improvise features after outcome.

## Independent verification

Production:
- imports committed SixLCU production evaluator unmodified;
- reconstructs complete n=2 instances, QG-15b frozen features and exact gap census.

Generic ORION:
- independently derives/evaluates SixLCU partition costs from the committed production formulas or independently reimplements the QG-4 cost semantics;
- reconstructs `Delta`, label cells and feature cells without importing production QG-33 results.

Native ORION-Q:
- authorizes only label-vs-value quotient statements on the declared domain.

Workflow requires deterministic replay and a self-consistent witness/value-sufficiency tamper rejection.

## Hard boundaries

- no all-n value theorem from n=2 census;
- no claim the one-literal predicate is globally minimal outside QG-15b's frozen language/domain;
- no generic abstract-interpretation novelty;
- no physical quantum advantage.

## Donor subtraction

Sufficient statistics, label-vs-value state separation and feature-cell irreducibility are donor concepts. Candidate value is the exact SixLCU instantiation and cross-family authority boundary.

