Protected QG-33 run is GREEN and the exact result is now sealed on branch `codex/orion-qg-qg33-sixlcu-label-value-20260822` as `research/extensions/orion-qg/QG33_SIXLCU_LABEL_VALUE_RESULTS.json` (result digest `64b8c8f85bd07086fc92671b2ec8e353bd927983db2173a801096f1d597350d3`).

Earned bounded result on the complete frozen SixLCU n=2 domain (38,760 instances):
- one-literal donor-optimal label abstraction remains exact for its label query but is **not exact-value sufficient** for `Delta=C_U-C_F`;
- 17 exact Delta values occur; the canonical same-label witness has Delta 12 vs 6;
- the full frozen 11-feature vector has 310 cells, 8 mixed-Delta cells, and irreducible exact-value error floor 411;
- canonical mixed full-feature cell has Delta histogram {4:252, 5:72};
- the prior bounded-gain surrogate is complete on 32,391 instances and incomplete on 6,369, so it remains diagnostic only and has no exact-value authority.

Independent generic ORION reconstructed all 203 partition costs and reproduced the full histogram/cell/floor result exactly; native gate, deterministic replay, and self-consistent semantic tamper rejection all passed. Stronger boundaries remain false: no all-n value theorem, no global predicate minimality, no new feature-vocabulary authority, no novelty/physical-advantage claim.
